{"id":"39","method":"turn/start","params":{"approvalPolicy":"never","cwd":"/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/repo","input":[{"text":"The reviewer found issues in your patch for commit e3f24674723e035ee00e32427df56f92a1d3f78b.\nI’m checking the mediated bundle for the final patched code paths and tests, with review focused on behavior introduced by `user-2` rather than unrelated existing code.\n\nThe patched terminal path hooks colon command execution before workspace command parsing, and the harness mirrors that behavior. I’m reading the surrounding input state transitions now to see whether the change accidentally bypasses any existing prompt semantics.\n\nSo far I don’t see a functional regression in the added routing itself. One review rule is still material here: this is an agent-facing terminal send path, so I’m checking whether the recorded validation includes the required real-agent smoke evidence.\n\nThe source context records only `cargo test --test ui_harness --test terminal_app slash_command` against fake/test backends. I’m getting exact source line numbers for the affected agent send hook before writing the review finding.\n\nFINDINGS\n\n- [P1] Missing required real-agent verification for an agent-facing send-path change. The patch routes colon-prompt slash commands through `src/terminal_app.rs:629` into `WorkLeafController::send_message` at `src/workspace.rs:245`, so it affects terminal chat behavior and backend agent messaging. The recorded validation only includes fake/harness coverage: `cargo test --test ui_harness --test terminal_app slash_command`, with tests at `tests/terminal_app.rs:71` and `tests/ui_harness.rs:356`. To resolve this, provide the exact real-agent scenario run and the visible backend response, or the exact pre-agent Codex initialization/auth blocker if the smoke check cannot start.\n\nPlease fix the patch's code or test defects through the orchestrator patch flow. If a finding is about missing verification, missing explanation, or another non-code issue, resolve it by replying with the exact evidence, command result, real-agent scenario, or blocker; do not submit a cosmetic patch for non-code evidence. Do not modify documentation or plain-text files; documentation and prose updates are deferred to the linearize agent. Emit `@work-leaf done` when the findings are resolved.","type":"text"}],"model":"gpt-5.5","sandboxPolicy":{"type":"readOnly"},"threadId":"01a04347-3072-7a22-9d9a-cf36a097865f"}}
