{"id":"95","method":"turn/start","params":{"approvalPolicy":"never","cwd":"/tmp/work-leaf-fair-normal-pilot-runtime-ad016ca/work-leaf/work-leaf-3feature-bench.HiRlMA/repo","input":[{"text":"The reviewer found issues in your patch for commit 958d0887669e2c5fa20adce9aad75a1128a71b7b.\nI found one concrete behavior issue in the cumulative patch and I’m checking exact file-relative line numbers from the mediated bundle now. After that I’ll return the review in the required `FINDINGS` format.\n\nFINDINGS\n\n- `src/ui.rs:980`: left-pane visual mode uses `control_selected` as the rendered row, but `left_pane_lines()` also inserts metadata rows for files and agent links at `src/ui.rs:1027` and `src/ui.rs:1041`. When the focused selection is an agent after another agent with metadata, `v`/`V`/Ctrl-V starts on the previous agent’s metadata instead of the focused agent row, so yanking copies the wrong text. The selected agent needs to be mapped to its actual rendered left-pane row.\n\n- `src/ui.rs:386`: mouse clicks are handled before the visual-mode key path, and `handle_mouse_click` at `src/ui.rs:1134` changes mode/focus without clearing `visual_selection`. Rendering still applies `visual_selection_range` at `src/ui.rs:1081`, so clicking out of visual mode leaves stale highlighted text even though the UI is no longer in visual mode. Clear the visual selection when mouse input exits visual mode.\n\n- Missing required real-agent verification: the source context only shows `cargo test visual --all-targets --all-features` passing. This patch changes terminal chat/pane behavior, so the review evidence needs either an exact real-agent scenario and visible result, or the exact pre-agent blocker from the bounded Codex smoke workflow.\n\nPlease fix the patch's code or test defects through the orchestrator patch flow. If a finding is about missing verification, missing explanation, or another non-code issue, resolve it by replying with the exact evidence, command result, real-agent scenario, or blocker; do not submit a cosmetic patch for non-code evidence. Do not modify documentation or plain-text files; documentation and prose updates are deferred to the linearize agent. Emit `@work-leaf done` when the findings are resolved.","type":"text"}],"model":"gpt-5.5","sandboxPolicy":{"type":"readOnly"},"threadId":"01a04347-1d9c-76c2-ac69-dc636dc8b712"}}
